WEBVTT

01:00.000 --> 01:14.480
You know how.

01:24.820 --> 01:25.040
These.

01:25.040 --> 01:31.040
All the bad news I like old late Crickey from back home.

01:31.040 --> 01:35.040
In search for a fact. What do you suppose that Noah California around here?

01:35.040 --> 01:36.040
We'll soon find out.

01:36.040 --> 01:39.040
Jib, Dog, Dog! Will you come out here and let me in?

01:39.040 --> 01:41.040
Jib!

01:41.040 --> 01:43.040
Jib!

01:43.040 --> 01:45.040
Well this is a surprise!

01:45.040 --> 01:47.040
Grannie! You little old fox of mule!

01:47.040 --> 01:50.040
Grannie! You little old fox of mule!

01:50.040 --> 01:55.040
Hey! Hey! Hey! You ain't changed a bit, has you, Jed, huh?

01:55.040 --> 01:58.040
No bigger in a minute than scrappy as a fanged head!

01:58.040 --> 02:00.040
Hey, look who's here.

02:00.040 --> 02:03.040
Howdy there, Mr. Crank. Sure he's good to see you.

02:03.040 --> 02:07.040
Every big time. Your ass pretty, and a fistful of pink holly on it.

02:07.040 --> 02:11.040
Yes, sir, Jed, everybody always did say we had the few prettiest girls in the hill.

02:11.040 --> 02:12.040
How are you? Is Ed Edd still with you?

02:12.040 --> 02:16.040
You bet he is. Hey, where's Jef, bro? He ain't home from school yet.

02:16.040 --> 02:18.040
How about Lori? Bring her along.

02:18.040 --> 02:20.040
Oh, I had to leave my woman home to do the chores, Granny.

02:20.040 --> 02:25.040
Ruth needed patching, Whale caved in, had to be dogged out, Mule needed to chew him up and little things like that.

02:25.040 --> 02:29.040
You know, we get four gullyjumpers. We don't roost high on the hill like you folks.

02:29.040 --> 02:32.040
But Ed Edd ain't out in the corner, Mrs. Cranky.

02:32.040 --> 02:34.040
Had to leave my woman to home, Ellie Mae.

02:34.040 --> 02:37.040
And Ed Edd, she's over at the motel unpacking and purtying herself up.

02:37.040 --> 02:39.040
Motel?

02:39.040 --> 02:43.040
Well, wait. We got plenty of room to take care of you and Ed Edd right here.

02:43.040 --> 02:46.040
Well, now, Jed, you know I ain't wanting to trade on a friendship.

02:46.040 --> 02:52.040
Of course, after Jef, Roe, and Eddi Bell's proper itch, then we're going to be wanting to live near our kinfolk.

02:52.040 --> 02:53.040
Kids!

02:53.040 --> 02:55.040
Ed Edd, Roe, and Eddi Bell?

02:55.040 --> 02:59.040
You mean you don't know what that boy's been up to?

02:59.040 --> 03:02.040
No, I can't say that I knew, Lee.

03:02.040 --> 03:06.040
And we's got some talking to do, man to man.

03:06.040 --> 03:09.040
Come on, Annie. We'll make a pot of coffee.

03:09.040 --> 03:16.040
Well, you've got a couple of fine women, folks, there.

03:16.040 --> 03:19.040
I reckon you're as proud of them as I am of mine.

03:19.040 --> 03:25.040
I reckon you want a sea ride done by Ellie Mae just the same as I'd want a sea ride done by Ed Edd.

03:25.040 --> 03:30.040
I reckon you wouldn't want no young man playing fast and loose with her feelings.

03:30.040 --> 03:33.040
I reckon a man's daughter's got the body.

03:33.040 --> 03:37.040
Well, suppose when you start blowing on the fur and get to the hide, what are you trying to say?

03:37.040 --> 03:40.040
It's going to come easy, Sam, what I've got to...

03:40.040 --> 03:42.040
Well, let's go ahead and sit down and give it a try.

03:42.040 --> 03:50.040
Ooh, yeesh.

03:50.040 --> 03:54.040
Ah, you've got yourself a regular power scare, you've got...

03:54.040 --> 04:00.040
Oh, I'd better take off my trotter, I don't want to get your face caught in those boots.

04:00.040 --> 04:07.040
Well, you can leave everything on, Lace, and sit down and speak your piece.

04:07.040 --> 04:13.040
Holy ma, sure do be setting on the stomp now, don't you?

04:13.040 --> 04:16.040
I guess you've got this here can stuffed full of money, huh, J.S.?

04:16.040 --> 04:19.040
Huh? Huh? Huh?

04:19.040 --> 04:24.040
Yeah, Lace, now, uh, hot Jethro and Esabelle.

04:24.040 --> 04:30.040
To speak plain out, your Jethro's going to grab the hook to my Esabelle's heart.

04:30.040 --> 04:36.040
I don't recall Jethro mentioning Esabelle's name since, uh, way last summer when she won that beauty contest.

04:36.040 --> 04:38.040
That's when it happened.

04:38.040 --> 04:39.040
What happened?

04:39.040 --> 04:40.040
This happened.

04:40.040 --> 04:44.040
Love letters, wrote by your Jethro to my Esabelle.

04:44.040 --> 04:45.040
Love letters?

04:45.040 --> 04:49.040
Steaming hot love letters.

04:49.040 --> 04:52.040
Someday I got to have a long talk with that boy.

04:52.040 --> 04:54.040
Let me see the letters.

04:54.040 --> 04:56.040
Jethro, I had better.

04:56.040 --> 05:00.040
You having a pretty sweet innocent young daughter of your own?

05:00.040 --> 05:03.040
You might just anger up to the point where you'd hurt that boy.

05:03.040 --> 05:05.040
Jethro got out of line, did he?

05:05.040 --> 05:11.040
Well, I wouldn't exactly call it getting out of line, provided his intentions is honorable.

05:11.040 --> 05:14.040
These letters was wrote way last summer.

05:14.040 --> 05:15.040
How come you just getting here?

05:15.040 --> 05:19.040
Well, now, I ain't a war or any money like you, Jethro.

05:19.040 --> 05:23.040
I had to scram from save to get to where I could afford to make the trip.

05:23.040 --> 05:25.040
Well, I'm a poor man.

05:25.040 --> 05:30.040
Only treasure I got's my little Esabelle.

05:30.040 --> 05:32.040
All right, lady.

05:32.040 --> 05:35.040
Not knowing what Jethro wrote, it's hard for me to speak.

05:35.040 --> 05:40.040
But I know he'll want to do the right thing, and I'll see that he does.

05:40.040 --> 05:43.040
Spoke like a two-hilled man.

05:43.040 --> 05:46.040
Why, I said to Morty before I left.

05:46.040 --> 05:48.040
Dry your eyes, Morty.

05:48.040 --> 05:50.040
Jed Clampett's a man on.

05:50.040 --> 05:55.040
I said he'll see that Jethro does the right thing by Esabelle.

05:55.040 --> 05:57.040
And I will, too, lady.

05:57.040 --> 05:59.040
You can count on it.

05:59.040 --> 06:01.040
Jethro, you sure got yourself a battle.

06:01.040 --> 06:04.040
I think you got more money than Big Head Bronx.

06:04.040 --> 06:09.040
I think Jethro's man like you is aiming to spend all that money on Jethro when he gets married.

06:09.040 --> 06:12.040
Him being almost like a son to you and all.

06:12.040 --> 06:14.040
I don't care if you're chicken or the hatch, lady.

06:14.040 --> 06:18.040
I want to hear Jethro's side of this first.

06:18.040 --> 06:20.040
Oh, you're a good man, Jed.

06:20.040 --> 06:21.040
Fair.

06:21.040 --> 06:23.040
Like I said to Esabelle, I said, dry your eyes, honey.

06:23.040 --> 06:25.040
Jed Clampett's a fair man.

06:25.040 --> 06:27.040
He's going to do the fair thing.

06:27.040 --> 06:30.040
He's going to see you married fair and proper to Jethro.

06:30.040 --> 06:32.040
And like I said to you later.

06:32.040 --> 06:43.040
Well, we're driving that truck, mighty shy on brains.

06:43.040 --> 06:44.040
That's Jethro.

06:44.040 --> 06:45.040
Fine boy.

06:45.040 --> 06:46.040
Jethro!

06:46.040 --> 06:47.040
Jethro, read daddy, boy.

06:47.040 --> 06:48.040
Jethro, Lacey says that last summer he wrote some love letters to his daughter Esabelle.

06:48.040 --> 06:49.040
Love letters?

06:49.040 --> 06:50.040
Boy, it ain't nothing to be ashamed of, son.

06:50.040 --> 06:51.040
Most natural thing in the world.

06:51.040 --> 06:52.040
I asked a boy like you to write letters to a beautiful girl like Esabelle.

06:52.040 --> 06:53.040
Them was fine letters, too.

06:53.040 --> 06:54.040
You should be proud of them.

06:54.040 --> 06:55.040
Well, thank you.

06:55.040 --> 06:56.040
Well, how come you're so proud of them?

06:56.040 --> 06:57.040
Well, I'm proud of them.

